.TH TEMP 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manual"
.SH NAME
temp \- display CPU thermal zone temperature
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B temp
is a utility that reads the system temperature from the primary thermal zone
device and displays it in a human-readable format.
.PP
The script retrieves the raw value from
.I /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp
and converts it from millidegrees Celsius to degrees Celsius.
.SH OUTPUT
The script outputs a single line to standard output:
.TP
.B Temp: XX.XX
The current temperature formatted to two decimal places.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp
The kernel interface used to read the raw thermal data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR awk 1 ,
.MR printf 1
